  "notes": "{指|さ}す is a godan verb meaning to point at or indicate something.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Takes を particle for the target\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- {指|ゆび}で{指|さ}す: to point with a finger\n- 〜を{指|さ}す: to refer to ~, indicate ~\n- {方向|ほうこう}を{指|さ}す: to point in a direction\n- {針|はり}が{北|きた}を{指|さ}す: needle points north\n\nHOMOPHONES (different kanji):\n- {差|さ}す: to hold up (umbrella), shine through\n- {刺|さ}す: to stab, pierce, sting\n- {挿|さ}す: to insert\n\nCULTURAL NOTE:\nPointing directly at people with a finger is considered rude in Japan.",
